# A saved login after the daemon restarts (cavekit-site-data.md R1, T-664): it fills the form again, and it lives in
# the shell's own profile, logins.json, with its username and its password encrypted by the engine's login storage (the
# file names the field, never the values).
id: site-logins-persist
section: Privacy and site data
item: A saved login is filled again after the daemon restarts; it is kept in the shell's own profile (logins.json), its username and password encrypted
shells: enyo mochi mojo
prefs: jihad.compat.trace=true signon.rememberSignons=true signon.autofillForms=true
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-login.html
kit: cavekit-site-data.md R1
fixture: site-data-clean
wait rect user 30
probe keep '(function(u,p){document.getElementById("user").value=u;document.getElementById("pass").value=p;document.getElementById("note").value="hello jihad";return "filled "+u;})("jihad-keep","keep-pass-9")'
tap go
expect dialog present 8
chrome dialog-ok
expect dialog answered 8
wait line 'logins: remembered for http://192.168.1.245:8077' 6
wait text sent "sent jihad-keep" 15
daemon-restart http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-login.html
wait text state "user=jihad-keep pass=keep-pass-9" 20
expect file APP/profile/logins.json encryptedPassword
expect file-lacks APP/profile/logins.json keep-pass-9
expect file-lacks APP/profile/logins.json jihad-keep
launch about:logins
wait text logins "jihad-keep" 10
tap 'sel:#remove-all'
tap 'sel:#remove-all'
wait text logins "No logins are saved" 6
